WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.083
We had heard about a virus.

00:00:01.083 --> 00:00:02.267
One of us had heard about it.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.429
We supported each other,

00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:04.934
and it ended up testing positive.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.779
And at that time they said 25% of people

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:08.834
seemed to be only getting
sick with this virus.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.349
So do what you do to
live your life healthy,

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:12.379
be good, come back and
see us again in a while.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.818
- Which shows that the lifestyle of some

00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:18.040
male homosexuals has
triggered an epidemic,

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.529
of a rare form of cancer.

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:21.016
- I went back about nine months later

00:00:21.016 --> 00:00:23.693
and they said that only 25%
of people were surviving.

00:00:23.693 --> 00:00:25.392
Meaning that everyone was dying.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.467
Which later evolved the next year into

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.033
100% of people were dying,

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.628
there was nobody that
was surviving the virus.

00:00:30.628 --> 00:00:31.946
- [TV Newscaster] The condition severely

00:00:31.946 --> 00:00:34.496
weakens the body's
ability to fight disease.

00:00:34.496 --> 00:00:36.146
Researchers are now studying blood

00:00:36.146 --> 00:00:37.726
and other samples from the victims,

00:00:37.726 --> 00:00:40.327
trying to learn what
is causing the disease.

00:00:40.327 --> 00:00:42.744
So far they have had no luck.

00:00:42.778 --> 00:00:43.611
- Hi, I'm Keith.

00:00:43.611 --> 00:00:46.778
And I've been HIV positive since 1985.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.694
So I'm one of those,
one of those survivors.

00:00:48.694 --> 00:00:49.894
I'm leaning up against a building

00:00:49.894 --> 00:00:52.425
where I'm about to go in and
get a Sculptra treatment.

00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:54.286
Sculptra is something
I've done several times

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.404
over the years, which has
helped with facial wasting,

00:00:56.404 --> 00:00:58.768
which is a result of medications from HIV.

00:00:58.768 --> 00:00:59.601
Hi!

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:00.434
- [Robert] I'm Dr. Robert Cohen.

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:01.853
Today we're working at Being Alive!

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:04.548
Which is a HIV/AIDS social service agency.

00:01:04.548 --> 00:01:05.942
We've set up a program called

00:01:05.942 --> 00:01:08.177
the facial reconstruction program.

00:01:08.177 --> 00:01:11.690
Earlier medications that were
used to treat HIV and AIDS

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:12.932
caused fat loss.

00:01:12.932 --> 00:01:16.050
They would cause fat
lipo-trophy, or lipodystrophy.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.669
Which manifests itself as a hollowness.

00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:20.598
Primarily in the mid-face area,

00:01:20.598 --> 00:01:22.681
in the temples, down low.

00:01:23.386 --> 00:01:24.925
People get that as they get older.

00:01:24.925 --> 00:01:28.071
But with the HIV patient
population it was a more acute,

00:01:28.071 --> 00:01:30.961
and it's a more severe
form of facial wasting.

00:01:30.961 --> 00:01:32.961
(music)

00:01:34.358 --> 00:01:35.862
- [Keith] You know you're
living with a virus inside you,

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:39.340
a lot of your friends die,
you've survived this thing,

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.661
and then it starts to appear on your face.

00:01:41.661 --> 00:01:42.552
It starts to show.

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:43.818
And all of a sudden you look in the mirror

00:01:43.818 --> 00:01:45.630
and you're seeing the
actual disease itself.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.024
At the time, I was acting and modeling.

00:01:47.024 --> 00:01:48.665
My agent, I remember, he
called me and he said,

00:01:48.665 --> 00:01:49.498
you just got a call from

00:01:49.498 --> 00:01:51.550
a casting director who wanted to know,

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:52.803
like, what's up with Keith?

00:01:52.803 --> 00:01:53.747
He's not looking like he usually looks.

00:01:53.747 --> 00:01:55.464
Is he sick, is something going on?

00:01:55.464 --> 00:01:57.214
And that kind of started the end of like,

00:01:57.214 --> 00:01:59.547
really the end of my career.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.280
- [Robert] What we've done,
we've put white cream,

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.709
and it's a numbing cream.

00:02:03.709 --> 00:02:06.955
The numbing cream takes
about 10, 15 minutes to work.

00:02:06.955 --> 00:02:08.240
It will numb up topically.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.149
I need to get the product into his face,

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:11.547
so for the first couple of injections,

00:02:11.547 --> 00:02:14.716
it helps make it more
comfortable for the patient.

00:02:14.716 --> 00:02:17.615
- It became kind of a terminal
death sentence automatically,

00:02:17.615 --> 00:02:18.975
and there's no medications for it,

00:02:18.975 --> 00:02:20.310
there's nothing to treat it,

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:22.366
and your own government
has turned its back on you,

00:02:22.366 --> 00:02:23.676
because it made it a gay disease.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.945
It just sucked, because
we were having to prove

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.527
that we were of value to
live in the first place.

00:02:28.527 --> 00:02:29.684
And the doctors had no cures

00:02:29.684 --> 00:02:31.311
and there was no leads on anything.

00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:32.974
And people were just dying left and right.

00:02:32.974 --> 00:02:34.532
You were choosing which funeral

00:02:34.532 --> 00:02:36.140
you had to go to on the weekend,

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.365
because you had to make a priority

00:02:37.365 --> 00:02:40.865
of which person was more important to you.

00:02:42.421 --> 00:02:44.412
- [Robert] This product
is called Sculptra.

00:02:44.412 --> 00:02:46.955
It's what's called the biologic filler.

00:02:46.955 --> 00:02:48.136
It's a chemical that will stimulate

00:02:48.136 --> 00:02:50.566
the body's natural production of collagen.

00:02:50.566 --> 00:02:52.202
We're going to inject the patients

00:02:52.202 --> 00:02:53.966
in the area that he, or she, needs.

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:56.499
And the patient will
wait for about a month,

00:02:56.499 --> 00:02:58.243
and they'll start to
see the collagen grow.

00:02:58.243 --> 00:02:59.483
And their face will be...

00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:02.585
The volume lost will be
replaced with collagen.

00:03:02.585 --> 00:03:04.122
It lasts about one to two years.

00:03:04.122 --> 00:03:05.748
- [Keith] I wasn't able to get a job.

00:03:05.748 --> 00:03:06.921
I was having these symptoms.

00:03:06.921 --> 00:03:08.572
It came to being alive.

00:03:08.572 --> 00:03:10.786
Literally just put my arms out,
stretched them straight out,

00:03:10.786 --> 00:03:12.433
and I just started sobbing.

00:03:12.433 --> 00:03:14.228
And I said somebody's got to help me.

00:03:14.228 --> 00:03:15.476
And that's all I said.

00:03:15.476 --> 00:03:17.239
They just put their arms
around me, on both sides,

00:03:17.239 --> 00:03:18.594
and just took me into the back,

00:03:18.594 --> 00:03:20.201
just basically, just helping me with

00:03:20.201 --> 00:03:23.110
whatever I needed and one
those ended up being Sculptra.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.860
Man, oh, get in here!

00:03:27.926 --> 00:03:29.022
- Well thank you for coming and joining us

00:03:29.022 --> 00:03:30.910
and letting me stick sharp
objects into your face.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.569
It always makes my day better.
(laughing)

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.376
- HIV is now what's called a
chronic maintenance disease.

00:03:37.376 --> 00:03:39.095
The patients now will continue to live

00:03:39.095 --> 00:03:40.591
a long and healthy life,

00:03:40.591 --> 00:03:42.504
a long and productive life.

00:03:42.504 --> 00:03:44.591
It is a disease and it
can change your life.

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:45.846
There's always hope.

00:03:45.846 --> 00:03:48.488
Whether it's HIV, whether it's diabetes,

00:03:48.488 --> 00:03:51.336
whether it's depression, there's hope.

00:03:51.336 --> 00:03:53.570
Take your medication,
talk to your doctors,

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:56.503
and most importantly,
surround yourself with people.

00:03:56.503 --> 00:03:58.246
Whether they have the same disease entity,

00:03:58.246 --> 00:04:00.878
or something else, and reach
your hand out and help them.

00:04:00.878 --> 00:04:04.301
Nothing feels better than
helping somebody else.

00:04:04.301 --> 00:04:06.279
And that's what we're here for.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:09.319
We're on the boat together,
let's help each other row.

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:12.152
(uplifting music)

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:20.414
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new channel!

00:04:20.414 --> 00:04:21.247
And now your part.

00:04:21.247 --> 00:04:22.191
- [Both] Subscribe here!

00:04:22.191 --> 00:04:23.774
- That was my part.

